      <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How hard should I tense each muscle group?</summary>
          <p>Tense to approximately 60% to 70% of maximum force. Never strain or clamp down hard enough to cause pain, cramping, or joint discomfort. The objective is gentle awareness of contrast, not athletic exertion.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can PMR cause muscle cramps in the feet?</summary>
          <p>Yes, curling toes too aggressively can occasionally trigger a foot arch cramp. If you are prone to cramps, gently point your toes upward toward your shins rather than curling them tightly under.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What if I fall asleep halfway through the routine?</summary>
          <p>That is the ideal outcome. PMR is designed to induce natural sleep. You never need to force yourself to finish the entire sequence if your body drifts off early.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Should I start at my head or my feet?</summary>
          <p>Either direction is effective. Starting at the feet is generally preferred for bedtime because it draws conscious attention and blood flow away from an overactive, rumination-prone head down into the lower body.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Where can I find an interactive bedtime somatic tool?</summary>
          <p>You can use our free, private <a href="/meditate/">Mindfulness & Body Scan Tool</a>, which guides you through a progressive somatic unclenching sequence with customizable ambient sounds.</p>
        </details>
